Hi Kevin,

For a Bayesian approach, Richard McElreath's rethinking package (which works with rstan) is another option - he has a few convenience functions to generate predictions from any models that you've fit (I've fit multilevel mixed models with the package and generated predictions to test against the original dataset, so I imagine what you're trying to do is quite possible).  Package user manual here <http://xcelab.net/R/rethinking_package.pdf>, forthcoming book here <https://www.crcpress.com/Statistical-Rethinking-A-Bayesian-Course-with-R-Examples/McElreath/9781482253443>.

Best,
Myfanwy

